# gemma4:e4b-tools — tool-calling tune of gemma4:e4b for local agentic CLIs
#
# Build:
#     ollama create gemma4:e4b-tools -f gemma4-e4b-tools.Modelfile
#
# Why this exists:
#   Stock gemma4:e4b ships with temperature=1.0. With a tool catalog
#   provided by the host (e.g. Copilot CLI), high entropy causes the model
#   to invent tool names that match its training priors but aren't in the
#   actual catalog — google_search, web_search, view_directory, ...
#   Dropping temperature to 0.2 dramatically reduces this confabulation
#   without hurting general chat quality. top_p / top_k tightened to match.
#
#   This variant is the default for copilotp, .aider.conf.yml, and the
#   opencode `gemma4:e4b` model entry.
#
# Notes:
#   - Thinking mode stays on (no Modelfile knob to disable it). To trim
#     thinking latency on the wire, pass reasoning_effort=none in the
#     request body (Copilot CLI doesn't currently forward this to BYOK,
#     but aider/opencode can).
#   - Re-run this Modelfile after `ollama pull gemma4:e4b` to refresh.

FROM gemma4:e4b
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER top_k 40
